---

<Layout title="Teaching">
  <Band tone="sand">
    <h1>Teaching</h1>
    <p>
      Helping other people understand engineering is a big part of why I do this work. Explaining an
      idea clearly is the best way to find out whether you really understand it. At the University
      of Utah, I was a teaching assistant for two mechanical engineering courses.
    </p>
  </Band>

  <Band>
    <h2>Computer-Based Problem Solving for Engineering Systems</h2>
    <p>
      An introduction to analyzing, modeling and controlling engineering systems with MATLAB and C.
      The labs build toward a class-wide competition, where students use kinematic models and
      solenoid-driven launchers to fire ping pong balls at targets. I was the head TA: I taught labs
      and lectures and graded assignments, labs and exams.
    </p>
    <h2>Dynamics</h2>
    <p>
      Dynamics is the physics of how things move, from a single particle to a spinning rigid body,
      covering Newton's laws, energy, momentum, impacts and a first look at vibrations. I was the
      only TA for a class of more than 100 students, holding office hours and grading.
    </p>
  </Band>
</Layout>
